; A node which says something true, written in a form the printer does not
; produce. Nothing here is invalid: it loads, it breaks no rule its type states,
; and it is what `dfcad fmt --check` is for — the gate's first stage, and the one
; a model acquires by being edited by hand.
;
; It is wrong in exactly one way on purpose. A node which was both unformatted
; and in breach of its type would leave a run unable to say which stage of the
; gate had caught it, which is the question the self-test exists to answer.
(node    site:S-001
        (label   "Meeting Room A")
    (kind Space) (type MeetingRoom)
  (geometry area)
      (frame frame:building))
